    "body": "Note on Expected's \"keep the coarser pass\" (M3, agreed with M5): it is not taken as a requirement as written. On #1536's sc_logo case a coarser pass that 'succeeded' imported the discontinuous corner blend with its jump smeared over at a 0.31 tolerance - wrong output. So a finer pass that trips the cap falls back to the coarser mesh only when that mesh is proven sound (closed shell, volume within tolerance of the STEP's own); otherwise the import refuses the face by name, as now. A smeared jump is worse than a named refusal.",
